@startuml InternalSecurityEnforcement
!include ../themes/dark-theme.puml
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
left to right direction

actor "Developer / Maintainer" as Dev
rectangle "GitHub-hosted CI\nPR validation lane" as GH
rectangle "Manual Approval Gate\nsecurity review + evidence" as Approval
rectangle "Approved Internal Runner\nJenkins / GitLab / Argo" as Internal
rectangle "Security Gate\nOSV + Trivy + image digest + Flyway + TLS" as Gate
rectangle "Artifact Registry\nimmutable digest" as Registry
rectangle "Production Cluster" as Prod
rectangle "Secrets + PKI\nread-only mounts + rotation" as Secrets
rectangle "Ops Monitoring\nPrometheus + audit + alerting" as Ops

Dev --> GH : push / PR
GH --> Approval : lightweight checks only
Approval --> Internal : authorized production run
Internal --> Gate : enforce actual deployment policy
Gate --> Registry : approve scanned artifact
Registry --> Prod : deploy by digest only
Secrets --> Prod : runtime keys, certs, DB creds
Prod --> Ops : security telemetry + rate-limit + audit data
Ops --> Approval : incident, expiry, drift, policy evidence

note right of GH
  GitHub-hosted CI is not the production authority.
  It is used for convenience checks and baseline validation.
end note

note right of Internal
  Only the internal runner or approved platform pipeline
  has the authority to enforce the production gate.
end note
@enduml
